----- stdout -----
bare-path — a backticked file-shaped path in markdown prose exists
Status: report-only

What it checks
  A backticked, file-shaped path in markdown prose exists, resolved against the file's own directory or the repo root. Shell/glob metacharacters, `NNNN` placeholders, and markdown-link labels are not treated as paths; a candidate resolving to a gitignored path is skipped as an environment artifact, and one matching an `external` glob is skipped as living outside the repo.

Config [bare-path]
  external (default: []) — globs matched against the backticked text for paths that live outside the repo, e.g. ["~/.writer/config.toml", "~/.cache/writer/**"]; a match is never a finding

Example finding
  bare path `src/missing.rs` does not exist

Fix
  No autofix — a finding needs a human decision

